### Describe the feature you'd like to request

Hey, pretty new here so I may be overlooking something. I'd like optional routers to be a thing. Basically as you combine routers, if there was a way to mark them as optional so that clients can infer they may not be served by the server.

My use case is to host a router that only works in development for serving some debugging information.

### Describe the solution you'd like to see

I would strongly prefer the client to not have to use any shared logic to determine if the router is being served or not. It seems like if we made the router under `trpc` optional, that would be enough.

server:
```
export const appRouter = t.router({
    users: usersRouter,
    ...(ENV.SERVE_DEBUG ? { debug: debugRouter } : {}),
});
```

client:
```
if (trpc.debug) {
    trpc.debug.getDebugInfo.useQuery(...);
}
```

### Describe alternate solutions

I don't really know other solutions that could work.

### Additional information

Right now if you try this in 10.x at least, you get `undefined` as the inferred type for `debug` in the app router.

I've also tried:
```
export const appRouter = t.router({
    users: usersRouter,
    debug: ENV.SERVE_DEBUG ? debugRouter : undefined, // @ts-error for assigning undefined to router
});

export const appRouter = t.router({
    users: usersRouter,
    debug: ENV.SERVE_DEBUG ? debugRouter : noopRouter, // @ts-error, type hint needed to infer app router
});
```

### 👨‍👧‍👦 Contributing

- [ ] 🙋‍♂️ Yes, I'd be down to file a PR implementing this feature!
